        "position": 2,
        "title": "Fits our Am Staff/ Pitt Mix Perfectly",
        "text": "Our 1-year-old Am Staff/ Pitt mix either escapes out of, or chews while wearing, most of his muzzles. We even tried ones specifically designed for his breed. This one differs from others in the basket design. Its one piece plastic molded basket does not permit him enough purchase to start a chew spot. It fits him well right now but may become too narrow as his block face fills out.The additional webbing strap that runs up between his eyes prevents him for kicking the muzzle off his face. Both the forehead strap and the behind-the-ears straps are adjustable. The webbing is soft and flexible making it more comfortable for longer periods of time. Added bonus: reflective stripes on the straps improve nighttime visibility.I like that my dog can comfortably drink water while wearing this muzzle. We primarily use it to prevent unwanted chewing and playing too roughly with our senior dog while we are out of the house. He is a well-socialized and friendly dog but still learning some boundaries.As an added bonus, we recently used the muzzle in lieu of the dreaded E cone (AKA the lampshade) when he broke a toenail. The muzzle is far more comfortable than the cone and does just as good of a job at keeping him from licking the area until it heals.",
